From 7386cc44a2a15c68b923214778b6a231c327c63c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:42:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add the fan speed
 function on Surface Pro 11

The Surface Pro 11 ACPI tables declare FAN0 (PNP0C0B) with a dependency
on SSH. Register the existing SSAM fan-speed client as a candidate for
this unit. surface_fan reads category 0x05, target 1, instance 1, command
0x01; it exposes RPM through hwmon and has no fan-control write method.

The command is verified in the Linux driver. A valid RPM response on this
unit and the independent cross-check are still required before release.
No platform-profile client or thermal-policy control is added.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
Assisted-by: Codex gpt-6.1-sol
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index a098cd5a6..990587985 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -411,6 +411,7 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp11[] = {
 	&ssam_node_bat_ac,
 	&ssam_node_bat_main,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_sensors,
+	&ssam_node_fan_speed,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_keyboard,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_touchpad,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_fwupd,
